  "description": "In Everything Nice—a variation on a classic Irish coffee—spiced rum takes the place of whiskey, lending its sweet, spiced caramel flavor to the coffee's roasted, bitter bite.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Freshly grated nutmeg, for garnish (optional)\n\nNotes: To make a 2:1 simple syrup, combine 1/2 cup granulated sugar with 1/4 cup water in a small saucepan. Heat over medium heat, stirring, until sugar is fully dissolved. You can add the syrup hot, since the drink is hot; any extra can be stored in the refrigerator up to three months, and often longer.",
